From 0ebc857c647dd17f812d8abf67fea44b3725a65d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas <nifri@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:37:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(templates)!: add Claude Code project standard for five
 stacks

Why: New projects should start with the same rules, tools and e2e harness, so Claude Code can work with little context and errors show up early.
What: common/ holds the shared layer (CLAUDE.md, agents, permissions, hooks, changelog, CI, init script). templates/{go,rust,python,typescript,flutter} add a flake, a Taskfile and a walking skeleton with e2e tests. The root Taskfile syncs common/ into the templates.
Impact: The old go and python templates are replaced, including generate-settings.sh. micropython is unchanged.
Open: nix develop and nix build were never run, the flakes were only evaluated. The flutter template was not executed at all. Details in README.md, section Test status.

BREAKING CHANGE: templates go and python have a new layout and need `task init` after `nix flake init`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
